and the government released its gross  domestic product report for the second  quarter this morning it showed the US  economy grew 4.1 percent from April  through June that's the best showing  since 2014 the US economy has been  growing for nine years making this the  second longest period of growth on  record CBS News business analyst Jill  Schlesinger is with us good morning Jill  put these numbers in context for us well  it was really an amazing quarter as you  said nearly the best in four years but  if we look even a longer term go back to  the year 2000 it's in the top 10 of  annual growth quarters that we've seen  since that entire time horizon  what really powered this was a  combination of effects number one we  know that those tax cuts really started  to boost business spending consumers  stepped up at a very good pace in the  second quarter the government spent  money and there's this really weird one  time and impact of the tariffs a lot of  foreign buyers wanted to buy US goods  before tariffs went into effect so we  saw a huge surge in soybean experts  before the prices started to change  rushing even before the door closes so  what does this mean on a longer-term  basis about the health of the economy  and more important for regular folks  well I think the health of the economy  is good but often we'll do these  segments and I'll hear from people and  they'll say gosh I don't feel like I'm  part of that and what's going on so it  is undeniable that growth was really  strong in the second quarter it has  picked up in 2018 but there is still a  lot of Americans who are struggling we  just have not been rising enough to  offset the impact of first the recession  and certainly now prices starting to  rise so we hope wages will pick up by  the end of the year still a very good  quarter all right Thank You Jill always  good to have you at the table
 

